# SALIS AUTO — app environment
#
# By default the app runs entirely on the design-bundle mock data (no server
# needed) — this is how the deployed GitHub Pages demo works, and how
# salisauto.app currently runs in production (verified 2026-09-17: no API
# origin is present in the deployed bundle). To point the same screens at the
# real API instead, set VITE_API_URL and restart the dev server (or rebuild).
# Login then authenticates against POST /auth/login and every screen reads
# through the HTTP repository.
#
# VITE_API_URL is the ONLY variable the app reads for this (src/data/
# repository.ts and src/providers/SessionProvider.tsx). `VITE_API_BASE_URL`
# used to be documented here — it only feeds src/data/auth.ts, a module no
# screen imports, so setting it silently does nothing and the app stays in
# mock mode. Include the API prefix: the client calls e.g. `/auth/login`
# against this base, and the server serves routes under `/api/v1`.
#
# Run the backend from ../server (`npm install && npm run dev`, port 3001 by
# default — see server/.env.example).
#
# If the API is on a different origin than the app, also add that origin to
# `connect-src` in app/security-headers.mjs — the shipped CSP is `'self'`
# only and silently blocks every request otherwise.
#
# Seeded demo login: `server/scripts/seed.ts` deliberately does NOT set a
# password hash for any demo account ("a seeded password hash in a
# repository is a credential in a repository"), so the `salis1234` password
# this file used to document does not work against a freshly seeded
# database — there is currently no seed/setup step that sets one. Set a
# password directly (e.g. via the auth module's password hasher) before
# testing login against a local live build.

# VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:3001/api/v1
